## 10. Data, Memory & Observability Layer

### 10.1 Market data ingestion

Read-only sources feeding the Market Scanner and Rug/Risk Analyst: DEX-aggregator pool/pair feeds (volume, liquidity, age), on-chain jetton metadata via `@ton/mcp` / TON indexers, and DEX-native APIs (STON.fi, DeDust) for quote depth. All ingestion is cached with a short TTL to bound RPC load and is treated as untrusted text for prompt-injection purposes (§9.4).

### 10.2 Decision journal

Append-only, structured log — the single source of truth for post-mortems and the 41-test-suite-style regression harness. Minimum schema per entry: `cycle_id`, `timestamp`, `agent`, `model_used`, `input_hash`, `tool_calls[]`, `output`, `cap_check_result`, `hitl_status`, `final_action`. Never mutated, only appended; rotated/archived, never deleted, for as long as any related position remains open.

### 10.3 Tracing & observability

LangGraph's native checkpointing gives step-level replayability for free; this is paired with a tracing backend (LangSmith or an OpenTelemetry-compatible equivalent) so that every graph run — including sub-agent invocations — is inspectable end-to-end, which matters both for debugging and as the audit trail referenced in the treatment of prompt-injection risk as a governance/compliance surface, not only a technical one.

### 10.4 Metrics & alerting

Circuit-breaker state transitions, cap-check rejection rates, RPC-provider failover events, and exit-policy triggers are all metric-emitting events routed to the same Telegram channel used for approvals, tiered by severity (info digest vs. immediate alert).

